---
/**
 * The "keep MERGIFY_TOKEN out of the uploaded pipeline" note shared by every
 * Buildkite snippet in the docs.
 *
 * `buildkite-agent pipeline upload` interpolates `${VAR}` before the pipeline
 * is stored, and it does so for the YAML it reads on stdin too, so a pipeline
 * generated by a script is no safer than a checked-in one. Escaping as
 * `$$MERGIFY_TOKEN` is not a workaround for the plugin property: plugin config
 * reaches the hooks verbatim, so the plugin would receive the literal string
 * `$MERGIFY_TOKEN` and use it as the token.
 *
 * The v4 sentence is what the agent itself prints on upload; Buildkite's CLI
 * reference documents `--reject-secrets` but not the version it flips in, so
 * the claim is attributed to the warning rather than linked to that page.
 *
 * `plugin={false}` drops the `token:` clause on pages whose Buildkite snippet
 * uses a native reporter and no plugin at all.
 */
import Aside from '~/components/Aside.astro';

export interface Props {
  plugin?: boolean;
}
const { plugin = true } = Astro.props as Props;
---

<Aside type="caution" title="Keep the token out of the pipeline you upload">
  <p>
    Set <code>MERGIFY_TOKEN</code> in the environment of the agents running your steps:
    <a href="https://buildkite.com/docs/pipelines/security/secrets/buildkite-secrets"
      >Buildkite secrets</a
    >, a secrets plugin backed by your own secrets store, or an agent <code>environment</code> hook that
    exports it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not put the token in the pipeline itself. <code>buildkite-agent pipeline upload</code> interpolates
    <code>{'${MERGIFY_TOKEN}'}</code> before the pipeline is stored, including in YAML a script feeds
    it on stdin, so a token written into an <code>env:</code> block is uploaded in plain text and
    stays readable in the Buildkite UI and in build history.{
      plugin && (
        <Fragment>
          {' '}The plugin's <code>token:</code> property carries it the same way.
        </Fragment>
      )
    } The agent warns about it on upload, and says that rejecting such uploads becomes the default in
    Buildkite Agent v4.
  </p>
</Aside>
